#### 9. Eager Test
**Test:** `OrderProcessor_FullWorkflow_Succeeds` (lines 57-63)
```csharp
processor.ValidateOrder(order);
processor.CalculateTotal(order);
processor.ApplyDiscount(order, "SAVE10");
processor.ReserveInventory(order);
processor.ProcessPayment(order, new CreditCard("4111111111111111"));
processor.SendConfirmation(order);
processor.UpdateOrderHistory(order);
```
7 distinct production methods in one test. When this fails, any of the 7 calls could be the culprit.

**Fix:** Either decompose into focused unit tests for each step, or — if this is intentionally an integration/workflow test — mark it with `[TestCategory("Integration")]` so the scope is explicit, and add intermediate assertions:
```csharp
[TestCategory("Integration")]
[TestMethod]
public void OrderProcessor_FullWorkflow_Succeeds() { ... }
```

